{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-js","path":"/2013-07-08-ecmascript-internationalization-api-specification/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"title":"kevinhakanson.com","description":"Kevin Hakanson's Blog","siteUrl":"https://kevinhakanson.com","social":{"twitter":"hakanson"},"author":"Kevin Hakanson"}},"markdownRemark":{"id":"55533b61-5ab2-5889-89eb-e03313d3faff","excerpt":"I recently downloaded and installed Windows 8.1 Preview to take a look at IE 11 Preview and check out the new “web standards” based features.  One of these…","html":"<p>I recently downloaded and installed Windows 8.1 Preview to take a look at IE 11 Preview and check out the new “web standards” based features.  One of these standards supported is <a href=\"http://ecma-international.org/publications/standards/Ecma-402.htm\">Ecma-402</a> or the <a href=\"http://www.ecma-international.org/ecma-402/1.0/\">ECMAScript Internationalization API Specification</a> (see <a href=\"http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/ff405926(v=vs.85).aspx\">Internet Explorer Standards Support Documents</a> for the full list).  If you don’t want to read through the specification, <a href=\"http://norbertlindenberg.com/2012/12/ecmascript-internationalization-api/\">Norbert’s Corner</a> has a December 2012 article explaining the API.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://test262.ecmascript.org/testcases_intl402.html\">ECMAScript Internationalization test402</a> hosts a set of runnable test cases to test the JavaScript implementation against the API specification. I was curious how well IE 11 stood up against the other browsers.</p>\n<p>For a baseline, here are the results for Google Chrome (Mac; Version 27.0.1453.116)</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 590px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/19d550ec0765a89d94b473499810225b/01dae/chrome-mac.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 9.45945945945946%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABQAAAACCAIAAADXZGvcAAAACXBIWXMAAAsSAAALEgHS3X78AAAAhUlEQVQI1wF6AIX/APjKevjLfffJe/fJevLGe+S8d+W8d+a9dvnLfPfJfPfJe/bIefzNg97lypjDkp7Ek6TImpzDkaDFlpjBjQDo4dbu593i29Ds5drj3NLi3NXm4dje2M/q4tnp6dbq6dnv4tj56d3g4d/f49/j49/18u31+fb2+PT09/TCxmB+k3ZySwAAAABJRU5ErkJggg=='); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Google Chrome (Mac; Version 27.0.1453.116)\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/19d550ec0765a89d94b473499810225b/fcda8/chrome-mac.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/19d550ec0765a89d94b473499810225b/12f09/chrome-mac.png 148w,\n/static/19d550ec0765a89d94b473499810225b/e4a3f/chrome-mac.png 295w,\n/static/19d550ec0765a89d94b473499810225b/fcda8/chrome-mac.png 590w,\n/static/19d550ec0765a89d94b473499810225b/01dae/chrome-mac.png 721w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 590px) 100vw, 590px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>So how do the bleeding edge versions of the leading web browsers compare?</p>\n<p>Firefox Nightly 25.0a1 (Windows; 2013-07-08)</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 590px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/35f4938a37a7835b71ab2053c6459cbe/37523/firefox-windows.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 8.783783783783782%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABQAAAACCAIAAADXZGvcAAAACXBIWXMAAAsSAAALEgHS3X78AAAAhUlEQVQI1wF6AIX/APfGc/fGcvfGcvXEcuO3bee6buK3bfTDcfjHc/bFcvfGc/TDa//UlcTewo66gpa/ip3ElJW/ipnBjZS+iQDw6d/r5Nvw6d/p49ro4trr5t/m4dns5t7v6N7y8OHt5t385dn06uLl5+Xk5+Xn5eH39fL3+vf3+fb2+fZ8s2BeEEPUJAAAAABJRU5ErkJggg=='); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Firefox Nightly 25.0a1 (Windows; 2013-07-08)\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/35f4938a37a7835b71ab2053c6459cbe/fcda8/firefox-windows.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/35f4938a37a7835b71ab2053c6459cbe/12f09/firefox-windows.png 148w,\n/static/35f4938a37a7835b71ab2053c6459cbe/e4a3f/firefox-windows.png 295w,\n/static/35f4938a37a7835b71ab2053c6459cbe/fcda8/firefox-windows.png 590w,\n/static/35f4938a37a7835b71ab2053c6459cbe/37523/firefox-windows.png 720w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 590px) 100vw, 590px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>Internet Explorer Preview (11.0.9431.0)</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 590px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/ac15f9eaf14b130b3bbf97140db1d740/073e9/ie-preview.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 8.783783783783782%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABQAAAACCAIAAADXZGvcAAAACXBIWXMAAAsSAAALEgHS3X78AAAAhUlEQVQI1wF6AIX/APfGcvXEb/bFb/LCb+C1a+S4bOC1avTEcPfGcfbEcPbFcfPCaf7Tkcjfw427gZW/ipzDkZW/ipfAjJK+hwDs5dzr5Nvu593o4dnm4Nnq5N3m4Nns5dzt5tzt8Nvs6N715Nr16eHi5eTj5uPk4d738/D2+vf2+fb1+PVWEl+/+mI5vwAAAABJRU5ErkJggg=='); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Internet Explorer Preview (11.0.9431.0)\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/ac15f9eaf14b130b3bbf97140db1d740/fcda8/ie-preview.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/ac15f9eaf14b130b3bbf97140db1d740/12f09/ie-preview.png 148w,\n/static/ac15f9eaf14b130b3bbf97140db1d740/e4a3f/ie-preview.png 295w,\n/static/ac15f9eaf14b130b3bbf97140db1d740/fcda8/ie-preview.png 590w,\n/static/ac15f9eaf14b130b3bbf97140db1d740/073e9/ie-preview.png 719w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 590px) 100vw, 590px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>Google Chrome (Windows; Version 30.0.1559.0 canary)</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 590px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/1f264d36342a5fbe96d106e0cc50732e/01dae/chrome-windows.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 9.45945945945946%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABQAAAACCAIAAADXZGvcAAAACXBIWXMAAAsSAAALEgHS3X78AAAAhUlEQVQI1wF6AIX/APjIePnKe/fIefjJevLEeOi8dum9deq+dfnKevfIeffIefbIePzLf+PlypjDkpvCkKTHmprCj57FlJjBjADw6d/x6+Ds5Nry6+Hr5Nrq5Nzr5d7q5Nvv6N/w7d7x7uDz59777eLp6ebm6ubm6OT08e32+fb2+fX1+PXmmGGgWbS6vQAAAABJRU5ErkJggg=='); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Google Chrome (Windows; Version 30.0.1559.0 canary)\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/1f264d36342a5fbe96d106e0cc50732e/fcda8/chrome-windows.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/1f264d36342a5fbe96d106e0cc50732e/12f09/chrome-windows.png 148w,\n/static/1f264d36342a5fbe96d106e0cc50732e/e4a3f/chrome-windows.png 295w,\n/static/1f264d36342a5fbe96d106e0cc50732e/fcda8/chrome-windows.png 590w,\n/static/1f264d36342a5fbe96d106e0cc50732e/01dae/chrome-windows.png 721w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 590px) 100vw, 590px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>I was a little surprised to see IE 11 come out on top, but not after reading <a href=\"http://blogs.msdn.com/b/ie/archive/2013/07/01/updates-to-the-internet-explorer-testing-center.aspx\">Updates to the Internet Explorer Testing Center</a> and seeing how many test cases they created, and are submitting back to the official standards bodies.</p>\n<p>However, given our customers still request IE 7 support, I guess I will be looking for a polyfill.</p>","frontmatter":{"title":"ECMAScript Internationalization API Specification","description":null,"date":"July 8, 2013","tags":["javascript","i18n","webdev"],"canonical":null}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/2013-07-08-ecmascript-internationalization-api-specification/","previous":{"fields":{"slug":"/2013-05-13-saturn-2013-software-architecture-conference/"},"frontmatter":{"tags":["architecture","conference"]}},"next":{"fields":{"slug":"/2013-10-17-the-end-of-chrome-frame-and-chrome-for-xp-support/"},"frontmatter":{"tags":["webdev"]}}}},"staticQueryHashes":["97908498"],"slicesMap":{}}